  "title": "Army\u2019s C5ISR Team Receives Award for Replacing Key Remote Sensing System in Record Time",
  "publication_date": "2026-07-27T08:47:34Z",
  "summary": "The U.S. Army C5ISR Center's Picketline team received the 2025 Major General Harry Greene Innovation Award after replacing a critical remote sensing system in record time. The team, credited with rapidly restoring capability, includes Robert Lutter, Nathan Nahm, Kait Kuzela, Adam Green, Jeff Bergan, Mark Fitch and Antwaan Thomas.",
  "content": "The U.S. Army C5ISR Center has honored its Picketline team with the 2025 Major General Harry Greene Innovation Award for swiftly replacing a key remote sensing system in record time.\n\nThe award-winning Picketline team members are listed, left to right, as Robert Lutter, Nathan Nahm, Kait Kuzela, Adam Green, Jeff Bergan and Mark Fitch. Not pictured is Antwaan Thomas. Photo credit is attributed to Sam Brooks.\n\nLeaders at the C5ISR Center recognized the team's rapid development and fielding efforts that enabled the Army to restore an important sensing capability with unusually short downtime. The achievement drew attention because rapid replacement of remote sensing systems can be critical to continued operations and mission readiness.\n\nThe reporting and imagery for this announcement were provided through DVIDS. The item, Army\u2019s C5ISR Team Receives Award for Replacing Key Remote Sensing System in Record Time, was authored by Brian Feeney and identified by DVIDS. The work is subject to the usage and copyright restrictions noted on the DVIDS website at https://www.dvidshub.net/about/copyright.\n\nNo keywords or tags were included in the original posting. The published notice lists the author as unknown in some metadata fields, while the article text attributes the work to Brian Feeney and DVIDS.\n\nThis recognition highlights the C5ISR Center's emphasis on rapid innovation and practical solutions that sustain Army sensing and communications capabilities during periods of equipment loss or transition.",
